      "label": "Description",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Pamphlet about civilian defense volunteer offices in the United States during World War II. The pamphlet includes information on the purpose and functions of a civilian defense volunteer office, how to set one up and organize it, and what the office does. It also includes a list of volunteer opportunities in the areas of civilian protection, unity, recreation and special services for troops and defense industry workers, consumer programs, health, nutrition, education, recreation and informal education, family security, childcare, service to single people, housing, the American Red Cross, food conservation programs, and war relief organizations. "
